# CMake build directories, generated compile DB, editor caches
build/
*/build/
build-*/
*/build-*/
# The bench tree is configured separately from the core one, so it cannot reuse a `build-*`
# name that is already occupied; `bench-*` is the second conventional out-of-source prefix.
# `NON_SOURCE_DIR_PREFIXES` in `tools/check_doc_citations.py` lists the same two prefixes for
# the same reason -- change both together, or a build tree turns the citation gate red.
bench-*/
*/bench-*/
# Below: the files CMake itself writes into an out-of-source tree, ignored by marker rather
# than by directory name so that a tree the name patterns above do not catch -- a throwaway
# `cmake -S core -B b` lands ~800 generated files in `git add -A`, which has happened twice --
# still stays out of the index.
#
# Read the limit of this honestly: a marker can only name a path CMake itself chooses. It can
# NOT cover a link target, whose name comes from the project (`bench_codec`, an extensionless
# ELF that matches no suffix rule here), nor any other project-named output. There is no git
# rule for "ignore the directory holding a CMakeCache.txt" -- static path patterns are all
# gitignore has. So an arbitrarily-named tree is only PARTLY ignored, and the safe habit is:
# name a build tree `build-*` or `bench-*`, and read `git status` before `git add -A`.
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
CTestTestfile.cmake
CPackConfig.cmake
CPackSourceConfig.cmake
compile_commands.json
install_manifest.txt
_deps/
# The Makefile generator writes one `Makefile` per directory of the build tree, outside
# `CMakeFiles/`. Safe to ignore repo-wide: this project builds only through CMake and tracks
# no makefile of its own (a future one would need `git add -f`).
Makefile
# The Ninja generator's equivalents.
build.ninja
rules.ninja
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
# CTest writes these next to CTestTestfile.cmake.
DartConfiguration.tcl
Testing/
.cache/

# Project-named build-tree output: not CMake-named, so the marker list above cannot reach it,
# but each path is still nameable exactly.
#
# `core/CMakeLists.txt` renders the compile-time config header (ADR-0068) into
# `<build>/core/generated/`, with a `drift-check/` copy beside it for the drift assertion.
**/generated/
# The package-config pair `configure_package_config_file` / `write_basic_package_version_file`
# render at the top of the core build tree. The tracked source is `core/cmake/*.cmake.in`;
# only the rendered `.cmake` output is ignored here.
libtracerConfig.cmake
libtracerConfigVersion.cmake

# Python bytecode caches (tools/*.py — the footprint/size gates)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Sphinx documentation build output + Python venv
docs/_build/
_build/
.venv/

# Doxygen XML generated for the Sphinx (Breathe) build
docs/_doxygen/

# Auto-generated each docs build (bench/gen_results_page.py) — never hand-maintained.
# Regenerated by CI before sphinx-build; run gen_results_page.py before a local build.
docs/performance.md
# Same reason: generated from a live ctest run by bench/gen_test_report.py and
# regenerated in CI before every Pages deploy. Tracking it meant the committed
# copy drifted — it advertised 21 suites and 24 vectors against a tree holding
# 67 and 36 — while the published page was correct. One source of truth.
docs/test-report.md

# ESP component: the release job vendors core/ into the component and packs it to
# dist/ for a self-contained registry archive — CI-only, never committed.
integrations/esp-idf/libtracer/core/
integrations/esp-idf/libtracer/dist/
bench/vendor

# ESP-IDF writes these into the example dir on set-target / reconfigure.
integrations/esp-idf/examples/*/sdkconfig
integrations/esp-idf/examples/*/sdkconfig.old
integrations/esp-idf/examples/*/dependencies.lock

# PlatformIO packaging fixture (tests/packaging/pio_esp32_can). The fixture IS
# platformio.ini + src/main.cpp; everything else there is produced by the
# `pio-esp32-can` job — the packed package under test, PlatformIO's own generated
# IDF project files, and the sdkconfig it renders per target.
tests/packaging/pio_esp32_can/libtracer-pkg.tar.gz
tests/packaging/pio_esp32_can/.pio/
tests/packaging/pio_esp32_can/CMakeLists.txt
tests/packaging/pio_esp32_can/src/CMakeLists.txt
tests/packaging/pio_esp32_can/sdkconfig.*
.merge_file_*
